From: skrimix <skrimix.git@fastmail.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: add OnePlus pogo pin keyboard driver

The OnePlus Pad 2 keyboard attaches through pogo pins carrying its power
and a half-duplex UART at 921600 baud. While unpowered, an attached
keyboard pulls a sense line low. The tablet then powers it, and the
keyboard sends framed boot protocol keyboard reports, consumer key
reports, touchpad reports with the layout of its BLE HID touchpad report,
and a status heartbeat every 100 ms carrying its brand, Bluetooth
address, LED and touchpad states. The tablet drives a transceiver enable
line while it transmits.

Follow the stock driver: power the keyboard once the sense line has read
low for 120 ms, register the input devices on its first status frame,
and power it off when it has been silent for 500 ms; then sample the
sense line to power it again if it is still attached. Report keys with
HID scancodes through a sparse keymap, so hwdb can remap them as for the
BLE connection, and send the Caps Lock LED, correcting it when the
heartbeat disagrees. Ask for the firmware version on connection.

On system suspend, tell the keyboard that the host sleeps, as stock does
on screen off, and wake it on resume. An asleep keyboard stops its
heartbeat and holds the line low, then wakes the tablet through the
UART's RX wake interrupt on a keypress. Wait for the line to fall before
suspending: the edge would otherwise wake the tablet as soon as RX turns
into a GPIO. A keyboard that does not acknowledge is powered off. While
no keyboard is attached, the sense line is a wake source.

The keyboard runs on its own battery, so cutting its power does not
reset it, and an asleep keyboard stays silent after power-on. Wake a
powered keyboard that has been silent for 500 ms.

Written from the OnePlus downstream driver (oplus_bsp_pogo_keyboard).

diff --git a/drivers/input/keyboard/Kconfig b/drivers/input/keyboard/Kconfig
index d8c64f333..a5320ab66 100644
--- a/drivers/input/keyboard/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/input/keyboard/Kconfig
@@ -486,6 +486,19 @@ config KEYBOARD_OPENCORES
 	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here; the
 	  module will be called opencores-kbd.
 
+config KEYBOARD_ONEPLUS_POGO
+	tristate "OnePlus pogo pin keyboard"
+	depends on SERIAL_DEV_BUS
+	depends on OF
+	select INPUT_SPARSEKMAP
+	help
+	  Say Y here to enable support for the keyboard and touchpad that
+	  attach to OnePlus tablets through pogo pins, such as the OnePlus
+	  Pad 2 keyboard.
+
+	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here; the
+	  module will be called oneplus-pogo-keyboard.
+
 config KEYBOARD_PINEPHONE
 	tristate "Pine64 PinePhone Keyboard"
 	depends on I2C && REGULATOR
diff --git a/drivers/input/keyboard/Makefile b/drivers/input/keyboard/Makefile
index 60bb7baf8..1adcaf313 100644
--- a/drivers/input/keyboard/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/input/keyboard/Makefile
@@ -51,6 +51,7 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_KEYBOARD_NSPIRE)		+= nspire-keypad.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_KEYBOARD_OMAP)		+= omap-keypad.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_KEYBOARD_OMAP4)		+= omap4-keypad.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_KEYBOARD_OPENCORES)	+= opencores-kbd.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_KEYBOARD_ONEPLUS_POGO)	+= oneplus-pogo-keyboard.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_KEYBOARD_PINEPHONE)	+= pinephone-keyboard.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_KEYBOARD_PMIC8XXX)		+= pmic8xxx-keypad.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_KEYBOARD_PXA27x)		+= pxa27x_keypad.o
